      <title>Chipmakers Post Longest Weekly Drop Since November</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/news/videos/2026-10-23/chipmakers-post-longest-weekly-drop-since-november-video</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">8ea710e0acd3a14acd67554b</guid>
      <pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 20:57:57 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>A resurgence in oil prices dragged down stocks and bonds, stoking concerns about inflation just days ahead of the Federal Reserve decision on interest rates. Brent crude settled near $117 as a flare-up in Middle East violence threatened supplies. Most S&amp;P 500 firms fell even as selling pressure on tech shares abated. A gauge of chipmakers edged up, but posted its longest weekly drop since November. The Dow Jones Industrial Average slipped 1.2%. Treasuries relinquished a portion of the previous session’s rally. Co-Host of Odd Lots, Joe Weisenthal says it's important to the US Economy that tech companies fire on all cylinders. (Source: Bloomberg)</description>
